{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 61, :comments ["<b>Cords of the wicked have surrounded me</b> — It has no parallel. One who says it is from the derivation of יאכל עד — it has no meaning, and its meaning is if cords have seized me, like the cords of the wicked that are fitting to come upon them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The cryptic phrase אין לו טעם וטעמו is rendered literally; the redundancy is preserved as Ibn Ezra's characteristic compression."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:29.665789679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}